{"id":"u-c20a509d-483b-4ca0-b49d-aba5cab21146","src":"community","title":"Prometheus Protocol","author":"Johnny W.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/ajyucW-unknown-for-now","desc":"Prometheus Protocol is a 12-week Olympic lifting focused strength and athletic development program built around the Snatch, Clean & Jerk, and Front Squat. The goal is to develop explosive strength, technical proficiency, speed, and power while maintaining muscular development and athletic conditioning.\n\nThe program uses a 5-day training week. Monday, Wednesday, and Friday are the primary Olympic lifting and strength sessions. Tuesday and Thursday use targeted accessory work for the shoulders, arms, forearms, back, and trunk. These sessions are intentionally kept secondary to the primary lifts and are ideal for pairing with swimming or other low-impact conditioning.\n\n## Program Structure\n\nTraining is divided into three 4-week blocks:\n\nWeeks 1-3: Progressive loading\nWeek 4: Deload and recovery\nWeeks 5-7: Progressive loading\nWeek 8: Deload and recovery\nWeeks 9-11: Progressive loading\nWeek 12: Deload and completion\n\nEach block progresses from higher-volume technical work toward heavier, lower-repetition exposures. The objective is not to grind through maximal attempts. Olympic lifts should remain fast, technically sound, and confident.\n\n## 1RM Progression\n\nProgrammed percentages for the Snatch, Clean & Jerk, Front Squat, and their variations are calculated from the primary lift 1RMs.\n\nAfter completing Weeks 4 and 8, increase the programmed 1RM for each primary lift before beginning the next block:\n\nSnatch: +5 lb\nClean & Jerk: +5 lb\nFront Squat: +10 lb\n\nThese are programming 1RMs. You do not need to test a true 1RM every four weeks. The increases provide gradual progression across the 12 weeks, and percentage-based variations will increase along with their associated primary lift.\n\nFor accessory movements prescribed by rep range and RPE, choose loads that allow good technique at the target effort. Increase weight when you can consistently reach the top of the prescribed rep range at the target RPE.\n\n## The Goal\n\nPrometheus Protocol is designed for the athlete who wants to lift explosively, move athletically, build strength, and maintain a powerful physique. Technical quality always takes priority over the prescribed percentage. If speed or technique breaks down, adjust the load.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Olympic Weightlifting","Athletics"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-09-21T04:34:07.599Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Monday (Pull)","Day 2","Wednesday (Push)","Day 4","Friday"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Muscle Snatch","sets":[{"r":3,"rpe":50,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Squat","sets":[{"r":3,"rpe":50,"x":3}]}]},{"n":"Snatch Balance","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":40,"x":3}]},{"n":"Snatch (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":40},{"r":3,"pct":50},{"r":3,"pct":60},{"r":2,"pct":70,"x":2},{"r":2,"pct":75,"x":2},{"r":1,"pct":80}]},{"n":"Snatch Pull","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":100,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Wrist Curls","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Wrist Extension (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Lateral Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Reverse Pec Deck","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"n":"Kelso Shrug (Chest Supported)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":4}]},{"ss":[{"n":"French Press","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Box Jump","sets":[{"r":3,"x":4}]},{"n":"Power Jerk","sets":[{"r":3,"rpe":40},{"r":3,"rpe":50},{"r":3,"rpe":60,"x":2}]},{"n":"Clean and Jerk","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":40},{"r":3,"pct":50},{"r":3,"pct":60},{"r":3,"pct":70,"x":2},{"r":2,"pct":75,"x":2},{"r":1,"pct":80}]},{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":40},{"r":5,"pct":50},{"r":5,"pct":60},{"